WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:03.002
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.605
I gotta say, you were
our first in-person guest

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.307
when we didn't have an audience,

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.342
and now we have a full audience,
so thank you for coming back.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.843
-Jimmy, the last time
we saw --

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.545
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.148
This is -- This is amazing.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.282
I mean,
last time we were together,

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.483
we were wearing body condoms.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.218
I think there were
ten people here.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.421
-That's correct.
We were like 20 feet apart.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:24.190
-They tested me in the lobby,
and I don't ever want to --

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.792
-We don't talk about that.
Yeah. Of course. Yeah. I --

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.527
-Good to have you back.
This is --

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:29.896
-Doesn't it feel good?

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.898
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.267
-I love a live audience.
I really do.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.635
-You miss it, right?
-I do.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.703
-You live for it. But, I mean,
that's why we love you.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.972
But I remember you said to me,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.740
"Jimmy, I got to be
the first guest.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.475
If you're going
back to the studio,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.876
I want to be the first guest."

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.878
And I was like, "Great,
but we don't have an audience."

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.713
You go, "I'm just gonna
do it just because --

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:49.615
Just for 'The Tonight Show'
and just for you."

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:50.916
And I appreciate that.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.886
-Man, I love you.
-I know. I love you right back.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.521
-Well -- Okay. So wait a second.

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.224
Usually,
if I were to be vulnerable,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.292
you would make fun of me.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.328
-And that's kind of
how our relationship goes.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.464
I say I love you,
and you say, like --

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.467
-Yeah, make fun of you.
But COVID's changed me.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.668
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.271
Now I accept the love,
and I give the love back.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.239
-It must be you guys.
-[ Laughs ] No, no.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.574
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.208
-No, I'm about to -- No, no.
-Thank you so much.

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:18.744
I'm about to make fun. Now I'm
about to -- Now I can make fun.

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:21.347
I do -- I do --
I do just appreciate you.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.215
And I -- But I want
to get into some stuff.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.118
"Vacation Friends," congrats on,
by the way.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.285
-We got to talk about that.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:27.586
-We have to talk
about "Vacation Friends."

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:28.821
-Or else the bosses
will kill me.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.356
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But I want to talk about --

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.958
We got -- Football is back.
-Football is back!

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.193
-It's happening right now.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.996
So, we got
the Bucs versus Dallas.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.231
I know you're a New England boy.

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:41.501
-Yeah, I was born
in New England.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.969
-Yeah, and so
you're a Patriots fan,

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.505
or a Tom Brady fan at one point.
-I am a Tom Brady fan.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.008
And just like Tom Brady,
I have moved to Tampa Bay.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.111
-You actually did.
-I was there first.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.811
I have this secret --
Really, honestly.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:55.281
I have this secret theory
that Tom Brady is stalking me.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.284
-Yeah. He's following you.
-We're both 44.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.886
I grew up in New England.
He moved to New England.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.188
-That's close enough.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.156
-We've both won
respective championships

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.258
in our respective fields.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.895
I moved to Tampa.
He followed me to Tampa.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:12.064
-I'm just saying.

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:14.267
Have you guys ever hung out?
Have you ever crossed paths?

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.068
-No, but I see these
weird security cameras

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.937
that have been stationed
around my property,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.405
and I think
maybe he's behind it.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.574
-Yeah, he's behind that.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:25.445
This summer, you came back
to WWE for SummerSlam,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.580
and it was honestly so exciting.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.982
-Dude, it was great!
I had a wonderful match.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.418
I finished second place.
-No, that's not the way --

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.421
No, no. That's not
the way wrestling works.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.756
I'm sorry.
-Says you!

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.357
-That's not the way
wrestling works.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:39.959
Roman Reigns.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.528
It was awesome, by the way,
just to see you back there.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.163
Because we talked,
and I was like,

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.998
"There's hints of you
maybe coming back."

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:47.933
And you're like, "I don't know."
Because you have --

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:49.702
You had "Suicide Squad."

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.637
You got the -- You had
the show that's happening,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.039
the series
that's coming out now.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.574
And you go, "I'm not sure."
Then what happened? WWE --

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.510
-I had a month off,
and they were like,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.245
"Hey, you want to come to work?"
And I was like, "Do I?!"

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.646
And they said that
live audiences were back,

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.748
and I love live audiences!
-Yeah, I know. So you...

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.884
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.853
But how did it feel --
how did it feel

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:10.790
to get back in the ring,
get the jorts back on?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.525
-Well, I mean, that was nice.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.193
-That was nice.
-You looked great.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:17.396
-There is no better feeling
than being in front

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.064
of a live audience.
There really isn't.

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:20.833
And I'm so grateful
to have all of you here.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.702
I'm so grateful to be back
with a live audience.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:26.171
There is no other energy
like performing and entertaining

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:28.041
or telling stories
or just shooting the [bleep]

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.608
in front of a live audience.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.344
-So thank you very much.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.246
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.848
-You remember --
Do you remember the first time

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.150
you actually wrestled
in front of an audience?

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.919
-Yes, I do.
-Where was this?

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.989
-It was in a gym called
L.A. Boxing in Orange County,

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.792
and seven people were there.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.828
And I was not good.
So nothing's really changed.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.929
-No. Yeah, right.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.297
But did you feel it?
Were you nervous?

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.865
What -- Did you come out
and you were like --

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.333
-Oh, man.
I'm nervous behind the curtain.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.767
Like, I'm always nervous.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.303
I think
if you lose those nerves,

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.339
if you lose that anticipatory
excitement, like,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.240
"Oh, I don't know
how this is going to go,"

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.608
like, you got to move on.

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.110
I think you're done
at that point.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.912
I think you should
always have that energy.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.613
-Because I know
you do love what you do.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.048
-Yeah, this is fun.
-I know.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.984
-We're just talking,
and people are listening.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.218
This is great.
-I know -- this is great.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:15.054
Or you're not listening.
You're texting. Whatever.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.623
-The people at home, yeah.
-They're not listening, either.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.425
-When you were --
-They're like,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.394
"Why is he interviewing no one?
Why is it just an empty chair?"

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:23.796
-They don't see you here.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.965
But this is before
you were John Cena,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.901
before you were a WWE superstar.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.237
You were known as...
"The Prototype."

00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:35.141
-I was.
Can you -- That's a --

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.575
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:38.577
-You were jacked.
-That's a crazy picture.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.613
So, that was taken
pre-cellphone camera.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.782
And that was a candid
by one of my friends.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.249
I had to cover up my man bits

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:46.252
'cause I was going
to the bathroom.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.953
-That is not true at all.
-That is not true at all.

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:52.057
-No, but explain to me
the name "The Prototype."

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:56.195
-So I was 50% man, 50% machine,

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.997
and 100% awful.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.965
It was bad. It was --
-It was a bad --

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:03.569
-It was bad.
-Well, I have video of you

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.405
trash-talking
and promoting as The Prototype.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:08.106
-No way!
-And you guys, judge.

00:05:08.106 --> 00:05:10.209
See if you remember this.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.345
-I look
in your genetic lunch box

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.980
and find a peanut-butter
and jelly sandwich

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.882
with the crusts cut off!

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:20.586
I am 50% man...

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.654
50% machine!

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:26.225
You are 100% fatality!

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.927
[ Growls ]

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.462
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.963
-A peanut-butter
and jelly sandwich!

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.399
-With the crusts cut off!
Come on!

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:36.902
-Come on, man!
-Come on.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.204
-What do you remember?

00:05:39.204 --> 00:05:41.274
-That -- So, that was done --
We were --

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.709
There was a documentary crew
following us around.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.778
And we usually have --
And this is done in --

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.379
That was in Southern California.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.649
But when you learn your craft,

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:52.385
part of that
is impromptu promo class

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.653
where they just put
a bunch of people in a room,

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:56.389
and the job is to try
to catch you off guard.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.824
And everybody
was kind of stumbling,

00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:59.958
and they just asked me to get
up there and say something,

00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:01.827
so I came up with that
on the spot

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.562
and threw it out there,
and they actually put it on TV.

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:07.800
So that actually -- that
"genetic lunch box" monologue

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.635
kind of kicked
the whole thing off for me.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.504
So I wouldn't be anywhere
if it wasn't for a peanut-butter

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.005
and jelly sandwich
with the crust cut off.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.506
-There you go. You're right.
Now -- Yeah.

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:15.808
-Weird story.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.910
-Look at you now, though.
"Vacation Friends."

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.344
This is the biggest original --

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:21.447
Hulu original film
in Hulu history.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.349
-People actually watched,
and they actually laughed.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.117
-It's really funny.
-And I'm so grateful.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.419
Thank you all for watching.
Thank you guys for watching.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:29.388
-It's so good.
"Vacation Friends."

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.491
They're making a sequel.
Already signed up for a sequel.

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:33.159
-Number two.
There's number two on the way.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:35.428
Which is kind of the story
of everybody's lives.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.796
-There's number two on the way.
-There's number two on the way.

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:39.332
Just waiting
for that next number two.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:40.966
-You have great chemistry
with Meredith.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.635
You had great chemistry.
Lil Rel, we know.

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:45.170
-Lil Rel's the best.
-He's been on the show.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.239
You know what I was
going to say to Lil Rel?

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.475
Because when I've seen him
do stand-up --

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.944
I saw him at this charity
he did for Denis Leary

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:54.313
called "Comics Come Home"
in Boston.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.283
And he was so funny,
but his laugh makes me laugh.

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.650
He's got like a,
"Yeh-yeh-yeh."

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.719
Or something like a weird --
He's got a weird laugh,

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:02.354
